msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:248
msgid "UTF-8 marker"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:249
msgid "Helps Excel show non-English characters correctly."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:250
msgid "Formula protection"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:251
msgid "Stops profile values from running as spreadsheet formulas."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:252
msgid "Keep export history / Delete exports after"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:253
msgid "Whether exports are listed in History, and for how long files are kept."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:254
#: templates/admin/settings.php:144
msgid "Allow exporting password hashes"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:255
msgid "Adds the Password hash field for administrators. Off by default."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:256
#: templates/admin/settings.php:145
msgid "Delete all plugin data on uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:257
msgid "Off by default, so reinstalling keeps your templates."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:264
msgid "Exports and imports touch personal data, so the plugin is strict about who can use them."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:267
msgid "Only users with the <code>list_users</code> capability (administrators by default) can export. Importing needs <code>create_users</code> and <code>edit_users</code>; Settings and deleting history need <code>manage_options</code>."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:268
msgid "Files are saved in a folder inside <code>wp-content/uploads/</code> whose name ends in a random 24-character code, and every file name contains another random 24-character code. Apache, LiteSpeed and IIS block the folder automatically; downloads always go through WordPress with a security check."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:269
msgid "The plugin tests the folder with an anonymous request to your own site and shows the result under <strong>Settings → File storage security</strong> and in <strong>Tools → Site Health</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:270
msgid "To keep files outside the web root entirely, add <code>define( 'USERFERRY_EXPORT_DIR', '/path/outside/public_html/userferry' );</code> to wp-config.php."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:271
msgid "Session tokens and capability data are never exportable. Password hashes are only available when an administrator turns them on."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:272
msgid "Every request is protected by a WordPress nonce, and all input is sanitized."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:273
msgid "The plugin never contacts other websites and does not load Gravatar images — the user picker shows initials instead. The only HTTP request it makes is the folder check to your own site."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:274
msgid "Imports are limited to 100,000 rows, 250 columns, 64 KB per cell and 20 MB for JSON files. Every part of an Excel file is size-checked before it is read, and a file that breaks a limit — or has values in columns without a name — is rejected with a clear message instead of being cut off silently."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:277
msgid "<strong>Nginx users:</strong> Nginx ignores .htaccess files. If the storage check reports the folder as publicly accessible, copy the rule shown in Settings into your server block and reload Nginx."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:284
msgid "Can I export users’ passwords?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:285
msgid "No plugin can export readable passwords: WordPress only stores a one-way hash. If you are moving users to another WordPress site, an administrator can enable “Allow exporting password hashes” in Settings; the hash keeps working on the new site. For anything else, ask users to reset their password."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:288
msgid "A custom field I need is missing."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:289
msgid "A meta key only exists once at least one user has a value for it. Make sure someone has filled it in, then click “Scan custom fields”. Also open the “Hidden & plugin data” group — keys beginning with an underscore are listed there."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:292
msgid "Accents or Bangla characters look broken in Excel."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:293
msgid "Turn on “Add UTF-8 marker to CSV” in Settings, or export as Excel (XLSX), which always stores text as UTF-8."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:296
msgid "The export stops partway through."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:297
msgid "Lower “Users per batch” in Settings (try 50) so each request does less work, and keep the browser tab open until the download starts."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:300
msgid "Does it work on multisite?"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:301
msgid "Yes, per site. Each site exports the users that belong to it."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/docs.php:307
msgid "All hooks are prefixed with <code>userferry_</code>. All PHP classes are prefixed with <code>UserFerry_</code>."
